'use strict';
/* Spoken lines, rendered with the Kokoro TTS model (Apache-2.0) by tools/build-voice.py from tools/voice-lines.json. Do not edit. */
const VOICE_TEXT = {"So you're the driver Nix vouched for. Bayhaven has more cash than sense, and I need someone with nerve.": "vera/0", "Hit the Quick-Stop one block north of here. Stand at the counter and hold E until the register pops.": "vera/1", "The alarm will bring cops. Lose them, then come back to the garage. Don't lead them here.": "vera/2", "Not bad. Keep the cash. Everything in this town can be robbed: stores, ATMs, wallets, cars.": "vera/3", "Hardline Supply sells guns and gear. Spend wisely.": "vera/4", "Smashing car windows is loud, and loud gets you caught.": "vera/5", "Buy a Lockpick at a gun store, like Hardline Supply. Then take a parked car quietly and sell it to Rusty at the chop shop.": "vera/6", "Rusty won't take a car while cops are on you. Lose the heat first.": "vera/7", "Rusty says you drive like a nervous accountant. From him, that's a compliment.": "vera/8", "ATMs on every corner and nobody watching them. Crack three. Hold E at the machine.": "vera/9", "Pedestrians will call it in if they see you. Pick quiet corners.": "vera/10", "Every store has a silent alarm and a camera. Pros switch them off before they touch the register.": "vera/11", "Buy Wire Cutters and a Laptop at a gun store. Cut the alarm box on Electro Mart's side wall, then loop its camera.": "vera/12", "Do it right and nobody calls anything in. It works on any store in town, not only on my jobs.": "vera/13", "Clean. Remember the alarm boxes reset after a few minutes, and loops don't last forever.": "vera/14", "Glimmer & Co. Jewelers. Two cameras, one alarm, and a lot of money behind the glass.": "vera/15", "Even with the alarm and cameras dead, the clerk will scream. Expect heat.": "vera/16", "Pick your getaway. The Ring Highway is fast, but they'll throw roadblocks and spike strips at you.": "vera/17", "Alleys and Forest Park hide you, but they're slow. Pick a dead end or let them cover the exits and you're boxed in.": "vera/18", "Somebody talked about the jewelry job. A guy called Marty, and he's driving to the cops right now in a silver sedan.": "vera/19", "Grab any car, catch him, and run him off the road. Don't let him get away.": "vera/20", "Marty won't be talking to anyone for a while. Nice driving.": "vera/21", "An armored cash truck is parked just north of Bayhaven Federal. The guards are on lunch.": "vera/22", "Take it, shake the cops, and sell it to Rusty. Armored trucks fetch top dollar.": "vera/23", "Next job needs a pilot. The flight school at City Airport, west of town, never locks its prop planes.": "vera/24", "Take one up, fly the circuit through the markers, and put it back down on the runway in one piece.": "vera/25", "Smooth landing. Now that you can fly, I've got bigger plans for you.": "vera/26", "This is the one. The Bayhaven Federal vault.": "vera/27", "You'll need a Thermal Drill. Cut the alarm on the bank's east wall and kill both cameras first, or half the precinct shows up before the drill is warm.": "vera/28", "Body Armor would be smart. Plan your escape route before you start drilling.": "vera/29", "SkyCash at the airport changes a fortune in foreign money every night.": "vera/30", "Cut their alarm, loop both cameras, and empty the desk. Then take the private jet and lose the cops in the air.": "vera/31", "A getaway by private jet. Bayhaven has never seen anything like you.": "vera/32", "Air Base Seven keeps two fighter jets fuelled. A buyer up north wants one, no questions asked.": "vera/33", "Steal a jet, fly the markers over Pine Ridge before they scramble everything, and land it on the runway. Expect company.": "vera/34", "The buyer's thrilled. And the air base is going to need better locks.": "vera/35", "The Federal Reserve moves cash out to the county by rail now. A steel safe bolted to the roof of the third car, and nobody guarding it.": "vera/36", "Catch the train, climb on, and crack the safe while it's moving. Then jump off and lose the cops.": "vera/37", "Robbing a moving train. I knew you were crazy, I just did not know how crazy.": "vera/38", "A friend of mine bet me nobody would ride the roof of the county train with the cops shooting at them.": "vera/39", "Prove me right. Stay up there for a full minute, then get away.": "vera/40", "I just won a lot of money. Here is your share.": "vera/41", "The feds traced the bank job back to my garage. We're done in Bayhaven.": "vera/42", "A boat is waiting at Pier 9, south across the Ring Highway. Every cop in the city is out. Just get there.": "vera/43", "Look at them standing on the dock. Bayhaven will miss us.": "vera/44", "Story complete! The city is still yours to rob in free roam.": "vera/45", "Name's Dixie. I run the duck pond and the ring toss, and the owner skims every dime we make.": "dixie/0", "His ticket office by the main gate holds the day's takings. Take it, lose whoever comes after you, then come back to me.": "dixie/1", "Ha! Let him explain that to his accountant. Come and see me again.": "dixie/2", "A sales rep parks his car in our lot every afternoon and never locks it.": "dixie/3", "Ride the Sky Wheel to the top and spot it for me. Then take a car from the lot and sell it to Rusty.": "dixie/4", "Rusty says hi. I didn't know he knew how to say hi.": "dixie/5", "The carnival needs a new act, and it's you, flying.": "dixie/6", "Land the Circle Jump by the roundabout, then ride the Big Drop to calm your nerves. Then come and take a bow.": "dixie/7", "The crowd loved it. Well, the ones who didn't call the cops.": "dixie/8", "Earl Pruitt. I pump gas and fix tractors, and the Mercantile has been bleeding this town dry for years.": "earl/0", "Their cash is behind the counter. Take it, shake the cops out in the hills, and come back for your cut.": "earl/1", "That'll learn them. Here's your share.": "earl/2", "A feller in the city owes me a truck. He won't be giving it back, so we're taking one.": "earl/3", "Bring me a ute. Any ute. Take the dirt roads if you like, it'll handle them.": "earl/4", "She'll do. Don't tell the sheriff.": "earl/5", "Dot's Diner. On a Friday the register holds the whole county's pie money.": "earl/6", "Do it quiet if you can. Cut the alarm, loop the camera, then lose anyone who comes.": "earl/7", "I'll miss that pie. I'll get over it.": "earl/8", "Sal Okafor. I look after the dam. Nobody comes out here unless they're hiding from something.": "sal/0", "Show me you can drive. Take an SUV into the badlands and land the Mesa Hop.": "sal/1", "Not bad. Not bad at all.": "sal/2", "Millbrook Fuel keeps cash in a lockbox for the tanker driver.": "sal/3", "Take it, and Dot's register while you're there. Then lose them out here in the canyon.": "sal/4", "Quiet out here, isn't it? That's why I like it.": "sal/5", "The news chopper sits at the airport most afternoons. Borrow it.": "sal/6", "Fly over the dam so I can get my picture, then set it down on the runway like nothing happened.": "sal/7", "Best photo I ever took. Here, you earned this.": "sal/8"};
